.TH NP_SOURCE 3 "June 2026" "netpipe v0.1.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
np_source_live, np_source_file, np_source_ring, np_source_free, np_pipeline_add_source \- netpipe packet ingestion sources
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <netpipe.h>
.PP
.BI "np_source_t *np_source_live(const char *" device ", int " snaplen ", int " promisc ", int " timeout_ms ");"
.br
.BI "np_source_t *np_source_file(const char *" path ");"
.br
.BI "np_source_t *np_source_ring(const char *" device ");"
.br
.BI "void np_source_free(np_source_t *" src ");"
.br
.BI "np_err_t np_pipeline_add_source(np_pipeline_t *" pl ", np_source_t *" src ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These functions create, manage, and attach packet capture and ingestion sources to a pipeline.
.PP
The
.BR np_source_live ()
function creates a source that captures live traffic from a physical or virtual network interface.
.I device
is the name of the network interface (e.g., "eth0", "wlo1", "any").
.I snaplen
specifies the maximum number of bytes to capture per packet.
.I promisc
is a boolean flag that, when non-zero, enables promiscuous mode on the interface.
.I timeout_ms
sets the read timeout for packet capture in milliseconds.
This source requires the application to run with administrative privileges (e.g., as root or with the
.B CAP_NET_RAW
capability).
.PP
The
.BR np_source_file ()
function creates an offline source that reads packets from a standard Wireshark-compatible PCAP or PCAP-NG file specified by
.IR path .
It does not require root privileges.
.PP
The
.BR np_source_ring ()
function creates a high-performance live capture source using Linux zero-copy circular ring buffers via the
.B PACKET_MMAP
option on raw sockets
.RB ( AF_PACKET ).
This allows capturing high packet-per-second rates with minimal CPU usage.
It requires administrative privileges.
.PP
The
.BR np_source_free ()
function releases resources allocated for the specified source.
Note that sources added to a pipeline via
.BR np_pipeline_add_source ()
are automatically owned by the pipeline and will be freed when
.BR np_pipeline_free ()
is called; the caller must not call
.BR np_source_free ()
on them.
.PP
The
.BR np_pipeline_add_source ()
function attaches an ingestion source to a pipeline.
When the pipeline is run, it will capture/read packets from this source and inject them into the processing queue.
A single pipeline can have multiple sources attached, which will run concurrently in separate background threads.
.SH RETURN VALUES
The creation functions return a pointer to a newly allocated
.B np_source_t
on success, or
.B NULL
on failure.
.PP
.BR np_pipeline_add_source ()
returns
.B NP_OK
on success, or a negative
.B np_err_t
code on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libnetpipe (3),
.BR np_pipeline (3)
